    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Saul had a concubine, whose name was Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah; and Ishbosheth said to Abner, “Why have you gone in to my father’s concubine?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA21:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "But the king took the two sons of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bore to Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Merab the daughter of Saul, whom she bore to Adriel the son of Barzillai the Meholathite."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA21:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "Rizpah the daughter of Aiah took sackcloth and spread it for herself on the rock, from the beginning of harvest until water poured on them from the sky. She allowed neither the birds of the sky to rest on them by day, nor the animals of the field by night."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA21:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "David was told what Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, the concubine of Saul, had done."
      }
    ],
